{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0146siPerUjhxmAkC4yVNsSw","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: «WORKING_AREA»/spec.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbbbbbbb-bbbb-4bbb-8bbb-bbbbbbbbbbbb","uuid":"a9b04ad9-2cf3-4cd7-9afe-5e0b4d117aa9","timestamp":"2026-09-24T02:41:01.095Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"«WORKING_AREA»/spec.md","content":"# Spec: Dark-Mode Toggle\n\nStatus: ready-for-agent\n\n## Summary\nAdd a theme control to the Settings page so users can choose between light and dark modes, or follow their OS setting.\n\n## Options\n- **System** (default): follows `prefers-color-scheme` and updates live when the OS setting changes.\n- **Light**: always light.\n- **Dark**: always dark.\n\n## Behavior\n- The selection is saved per user in their profile (e.g., `themePreference: \"system\" | \"light\" | \"dark\"`).\n- New and existing users with no saved value default to **System**.\n- Changing the setting applies immediately, with no page reload.\n- The preference follows the user across devices and sessions.\n- Apply the theme before first paint (for example, from a cached value) so the page doesn't flash the wrong theme.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n1. The Settings page shows a three-option theme control.\n2. The selection persists to the user profile and survives logout/login.\n3. System mode tracks OS changes in real time.\n4. All pages meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes.\n5. If saving fails, show an error and revert the control.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
